=   entry .Error   raised when delimited text cannot be parsed, or a row cannot be decoded
-     detail
+     detail

-         Error `↯/s.83.1`, with a subcode from its `#reason`. A **parse** failure, a quote found after
-         the start of an unquoted cell, reads _could not parse row data at row `row`, column
-         `column` because a quote was found after the start of a cell_, and carries the 1-based
-         row and column and the character offset into the input. A **decode** failure reads
-         _could not decode the cell because the cell was absent_, or _because the value `value`
-         could not be parsed as `expected`_; its position is not in the error itself (`#row` and
-         `#column` are `Prim`, `#offset` is `0`) but in the `CellRef` focus an accruing
-         strategy records with it.
+         Error `↯/s.83.1`, con un subcódigo que procede de su `#reason`. Un fallo de **análisis**,
+         unas comillas encontradas después del comienzo de una celda sin entrecomillar, dice
+         _could not parse row data at row `row`, column `column` because a quote was found after
+         the start of a cell_, y lleva la fila y la columna, contadas desde 1, y el
+         desplazamiento en caracteres dentro de la entrada. Un fallo de **decodificación** dice
+         _could not decode the cell because the cell was absent_, o _because the value `value`
+         could not be parsed as `expected`_; su posición no está en el propio error (`#row` y
+         `#column` son `Prim`, `#offset` es `0`) sino en el foco `CellRef` que registra con él
+         una estrategia acumulativa.

